Proof of Concept

1.  Simulate ingesting documents along with their Access Control Lists (ACLs).
2.  Store documents in a Vector Database with permissions metadata.
3.  Simulate a user querying the system, applying a metadata filter based on their mock identity.
4.  Generate a simplified, PM-friendly answer using an LLM.


Key Features V1 (MVP)
1.  Interactive Q&A Chat: A conversational interface where users can ask questions about technical concepts in natural language.
2.  Role-Based Access Control (RBAC): The system must respect existing company permissions. A user should only receive answers derived from documentation they are authorized to view.
3.  ELI5 Explanations: The AI must be prompted to return simplified, non-technical explanations focusing on business value, data flow, and dependencies.
4.  On-the-Fly Architecture Diagrams: The application will generate visual flowcharts and architecture diagrams (via Mermaid.js) to help users visualize complex systems.
5.  Source Citations: Every answer provided by the AI must include links back to the original engineering documents used to generate the answer.


Technical Stack

Language: Python
AI Framework: LangChain or LlamaIndex
Vector Database: ChromaDB (runs locally, no cloud setup needed for PoC)
LLM: Google Gemini API (or OpenAI/Claude)
Interface: A simple Command Line Interface (CLI) or a lightweight web UI using Gradio/Streamlit.
